{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived","id":601378,"title":"Heart of Re and the ascendancy of the Deceived","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-23T21:37:32-07:00","id":601378,"title":"Heart of Re and the ascendancy of the Deceived","content":"Do any of you all think that the Heart of Re Seba has the power to finally awaken those Deceived who have yet to rise since the time the temakhs were melded to their slaves? I am under the belief that yes, that Seba can... at the cost of raising and empowering all their enemies. At the same time, I think such an event would tip the the scales irrevocably in their favor, possibly giving the Akhem-Urtu the numbers and power to bring about a new &quot;era&quot; as it were. What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T21:49:45-07:00","id":601400,"title":"","content":"I'm less certain. I don't think the Temakh are infinite. All of the Deceived who are in action at the moment possess, between them, all the fragments of the broken Shan'iatu. Those Deceived who never awoke were not suitable hosts for the Temakh, and the nature of the betrayal during the Rite meant that the other Shan'iatu wouldn't have been able to tell the Akhem-Urtu Guildmasters to use the &quot;right&quot; Rite of Return for some bodies and the &quot;wrong&quot; one, the one that bound them into their servants, to the others. So when the first Sothic Turn happened, any vessels prepared to hold the Temakh who didn't have a Temakh became inert, and I can't imagine any magic can give them life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T23:39:10-07:00","id":601440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived?p=601400#post601400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm less certain. I don't think the Temakh are infinite. All of the Deceived who are in action at the moment possess, between them, all the fragments of the broken Shan'iatu. Those Deceived who never awoke were not suitable hosts for the Temakh, and the nature of the betrayal during the Rite meant that the other Shan'iatu wouldn't have been able to tell the Akhem-Urtu Guildmasters to use the &quot;right&quot; Rite of Return for some bodies and the &quot;wrong&quot; one, the one that bound them into their servants, to the others. So when the first Sothic Turn happened, any vessels prepared to hold the Temakh who didn't have a Temakh became inert, and I can't imagine any magic can give them life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that as well when it then occurred to me, the temakhs are compared to the seba, they are ultimately tied to patterns of Sekhem. I believe that it is incorrect to assume that the shards active were the only shards that exist... merely the only ones awake. As it is said,they whipped through all their prepared servants,and while yes not all of them &quot;took&quot;, I believe that there are fragments still within those bodies... they just need to be correctly calibrated as the sabotaged Rite had a faulty Sekhem pattern programmed into it. But as the Heart of Re provides a surge of Sekhem much, MUCH more powerful than what is normal (in giving all Shuankhsen Sekhem 10), I believe it is capable of &quot;fixing&quot; what was intentionally broken and waking those shards and their hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T16:38:01-07:00","id":604294,"title":"","content":"Well, it's certainly a valid interpretation for your own game, but it's not really how I read the original text.<br /> <br /> That said, running with the assumption that your description of events is correct, it would certainly be a great victory for the Deceived. I don't think it would upset the balance terribly, however. The Deceived are implied to have been the smallest &quot;guild&quot; to begin with, as their servitors were primarily just members of the Pharaoh's household. Even if they did rival the other guilds, they would still be looking at being outnumbered at least 5-to-1. And if it were to happen in this new era of surveillance and information sharing, there is a strong possibility that the increased activity on their part might finally wrest the Deceived from out of the shadows and into full view of Arisen society. A dangerous place to be when the numbers are so greatly against you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T21:19:35-07:00","id":604461,"title":"","content":"This may be my favorite thread for <b>Mummy</b> so far. Just reading the thread's title made it click in my head, but then considering that the other Deceived haven't woken up because they're not needed or something...<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if they're <i>broken</i>. What happens when the Deceived anticipate rejoicing their finally awoken brethren only to find out they're just as lost and monstrous as the Shuankhsen? Bereft of henet and the agony of the temakhs in Twilight, their souls were stranded for eons, corrupted not by Ammut but by the cold, black stars of the heavens. They lust - not for Pillars or mortal hearts - but for re-connecting to their more pure temakh versions.<br /> <br /> The void between stars isn't the Devourer. It is superego to Ammut's id. It is thinking, calculating. It is cold. It is <i>blissful</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 07-27-2015, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T20:08:06-07:00","id":605251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived?p=604294#post604294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's certainly a valid interpretation for your own game, but it's not really how I read the original text.<br /> <br /> That said, running with the assumption that your description of events is correct, it would certainly be a great victory for the Deceived. I don't think it would upset the balance terribly, however. The Deceived are implied to have been the smallest &quot;guild&quot; to begin with, as their servitors were primarily just members of the Pharaoh's household. Even if they did rival the other guilds, they would still be looking at being outnumbered at least 5-to-1. And if it were to happen in this new era of surveillance and information sharing, there is a strong possibility that the increased activity on their part might finally wrest the Deceived from out of the shadows and into full view of Arisen society. A dangerous place to be when the numbers are so greatly against you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> an excellent point, however, five to one is much more manageable than let's say 42 to one. And regardless, numbers against them only truly has meaning if they were mortal. As it stands, even as few as they are.. they are eternal. Apart from the threat of losing seba, they fare much better in the face of combat( more so when you take into consideration that many Deceived are perfectly apt at covert, asymetric warfare already). So I wouldn't be so sure that they would be overly disadvantaged apart for a few centuries of adjustment for the newly risen Deceived <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. You make a valid point though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T20:20:31-07:00","id":605257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived?p=604461#post604461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be my favorite thread for <b>Mummy</b> so far. Just reading the thread's title made it click in my head, but then considering that the other Deceived haven't woken up because they're not needed or something...<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if they're <i>broken</i>. What happens when the Deceived anticipate rejoicing their finally awoken brethren only to find out they're just as lost and monstrous as the Shuankhsen? Bereft of henet and the agony of the temakhs in Twilight, their souls were stranded for eons, corrupted not by Ammut but by the cold, black stars of the heavens. They lust - not for Pillars or mortal hearts - but for re-connecting to their more pure temakh versions.<br /> <br /> The void between stars isn't the Devourer. It is superego to Ammut's id. It is thinking, calculating. It is cold. It is <i>blissful</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very interesting, though instead of being beastial, what if they were emotionless puppets of Fate, to match the cold &quot;superego&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T20:33:11-07:00","id":605258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived?p=605251#post605251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an excellent point, however, five to one is much more manageable than let's say 42 to one. And regardless, numbers against them only truly has meaning if they were mortal. As it stands, even as few as they are.. they are eternal. Apart from the threat of losing seba, they fare much better in the face of combat( more so when you take into consideration that many Deceived are perfectly apt at covert, asymetric warfare already). So I wouldn't be so sure that they would be overly disadvantaged apart for a few centuries of adjustment for the newly risen Deceived <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. You make a valid point though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deceived certainly have an advantage in asymmetric warfare, and are going to need to continue carrying it out if they want to wage an effective campaign against the Arisen. The problem is that a large number of newly woken, inexperienced Deceived could give away as much, or even more, of an advantage than they give. A big strength of the Deceived is their mystery, but if a Deceived can be captured and broken and the secrets of Name Magic and Seba shared among the Arisen then the Deceived lose a lot of their mystical might. More Deceived give a lot more opportunities for that to happen.<br /> <br /> In regards to Deceived being eternal, no more so than an Arisen. The only vulnerability the Arisen have over the Deceived is that they can become Shuankhsen, and that's something neither side wants. Shuankhsen are the only thing in the setting that can provably cause the two warring factions of Deathless to put aside their differences and work together. Their respective variations on immortality thus fail to lend an advantage to either side, I would think. They're back to mucking with one another's cults and trying to prevent relics from making their way back to the Judges, in effect.<br /> <br /> I did say originally that it would be a great victory for the Deceived and my view on that hasn't been changed. I don't think it would be a game changer that would allow for a &quot;new era&quot;, as you put it, for the dominion of the Akhem-Urtu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:03:19-07:00","id":605345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived?p=605258#post605258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deceived certainly have an advantage in asymmetric warfare, and are going to need to continue carrying it out if they want to wage an effective campaign against the Arisen. The problem is that a large number of newly woken, inexperienced Deceived could give away as much, or even more, of an advantage than they give. A big strength of the Deceived is their mystery, but if a Deceived can be captured and broken and the secrets of Name Magic and Seba shared among the Arisen then the Deceived lose a lot of their mystical might. More Deceived give a lot more opportunities for that to happen.<br /> <br /> In regards to Deceived being eternal, no more so than an Arisen. The only vulnerability the Arisen have over the Deceived is that they can become Shuankhsen, and that's something neither side wants. Shuankhsen are the only thing in the setting that can provably cause the two warring factions of Deathless to put aside their differences and work together. Their respective variations on immortality thus fail to lend an advantage to either side, I would think. They're back to mucking with one another's cults and trying to prevent relics from making their way back to the Judges, in effect.<br /> <br /> I did say originally that it would be a great victory for the Deceived and my view on that hasn't been changed. I don't think it would be a game changer that would allow for a &quot;new era&quot;, as you put it, for the dominion of the Akhem-Urtu.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Again you make very good points. I do disagree with your views on their eternal existence and think you are looking at it too much from a short term perspective, but I completely understand where you are coming from. I also am rather certain that the threat of them being caught and broken is far easier said than done.. considering that if they are forced into such a dire situation.. they will unfailingly fall back on the protection of their temakhs through Blessed is the God-King third tier, especially if they are almost bereft of Sekhem. Would some be broken? With very great difficulty,but not in such a way that could hurt the guild in any real way- after all, they have recently risen, they know virtually nothing about the guild as it is now or how to effectively find Seba in the modern age. You are correct in that perhaps it wouldn't lead to some glorious new age of utter dominance, but I do firmly believe that by the time of the fifth Sothic turn, their guild would be much more powerful than they are now due to the avalibility of members. But the truth of the matter is that we simply have interpreted the book diffeently, and that is perfectly okay <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-28-2015, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T00:15:37-07:00","id":605355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/601378-heart-of-re-and-the-ascendancy-of-the-deceived?p=604461#post604461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be my favorite thread for <b>Mummy</b> so far. Just reading the thread's title made it click in my head, but then considering that the other Deceived haven't woken up because they're not needed or something...<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder if they're <i>broken</i>. What happens when the Deceived anticipate rejoicing their finally awoken brethren only to find out they're just as lost and monstrous as the Shuankhsen? Bereft of henet and the agony of the temakhs in Twilight, their souls were stranded for eons, corrupted not by Ammut but by the cold, black stars of the heavens. They lust - not for Pillars or mortal hearts - but for re-connecting to their more pure temakh versions.<br /> <br /> The void between stars isn't the Devourer. It is superego to Ammut's id. It is thinking, calculating. It is cold. It is <i>blissful</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Though to be honest, I am rather confused by the comparison of the superego to the black stars, clarify for me? Burnt out husks of malice and envy doesn't quite match up to a humans' sense of absolute morality and logical thought by my understanding lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}